# Agent workspace / IDE
# `.claude/` is the tool directory. Worktrees and session state are ephemeral and stay untracked;
# the dispatchable subagent definitions under `.claude/agents/` are tracked, because a subagent
# only this machine can dispatch is not a shared capability. Roles stay defined under
# `artifacts/agents/` and those files route over them rather than copying them.
# The reason recorded here until 2026-09-20 -- "a root .claude/ fails the harness gate" -- stopped
# being true when gate 4 gained TOOL_ROOT_DIRS; tests/test_gate2_ignores_nested_checkouts.py
# holds both halves of that, and the gate passes with this directory present.
# Excluded by path and then re-included by extension, so a stray cache under agents/ stays out.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
.claude/agents/*
!.claude/agents/*.md
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/
.agents/

# scratch and build artifacts
tmp/
# AGENTS.md is the only repository-level instruction file. A local CLAUDE.md is a
# contributor's own business and is never tracked here.
/CLAUDE.md

# The `state` slot of X: verified mutable truth, regenerated by
# scripts/reconstruct_state.py. Committing it would make it record its own parent
# commit and be stale from the moment it lands.
artifacts/state.md

# The derived cache: regenerated from the raw NWB files, 6.7 GB across 88 files when this rule
# landed. It was excluded only by the blanket extension rules -- *.pkl caught 66 of those files
# and *.json the other 22 -- so the directory itself matched nothing, and a cache file written
# with any other suffix was untracked and visible, one careless `git add -A` from the index.
# P-10. Excluded by path, so the suffix no longer decides. The extension rules above stay: they
# cover *.pkl and *.json everywhere else in the repository, which a rule anchored here cannot.
artifacts/developer/.cache/
